WEBVTT

00:00.420 --> 00:01.890
Oh, welcome!

00:00.520 --> 00:05.940
<b>A Nightmare Stained in Black</b>

00:01.890 --> 00:04.600
Here to pick up that order you placed?

00:04.600 --> 00:08.210
Yes, the Conjuring Ink
I asked for the other day...

00:08.210 --> 00:10.410
And there's a crack in my wand.

00:10.410 --> 00:11.930
Do you think you could fix it?

00:11.930 --> 00:14.360
<i>That flash of light was so bright...</i>

00:14.630 --> 00:17.500
<i>There's no way Grandpa didn't see it.</i>

00:18.360 --> 00:21.250
<i>Maybe Mister Qifrey
knows something about it?</i>

00:22.920 --> 00:25.950
<i>Or could he be the reason?</i>

00:34.260 --> 00:37.770
S-S-S-Sorry!

00:37.770 --> 00:41.020
Looks like that Grasping Wind seal

00:41.650 --> 00:44.570
was a bit too big to just
grab a mountain apple.

00:45.470 --> 00:46.540
Right.

00:46.540 --> 00:50.730
The first time, the seal was too small,
and it just made them wobble,

00:50.730 --> 00:53.230
so I thought I should make it stronger...

00:53.230 --> 00:56.440
How about angling the Sign of
Pulling so it makes a twist?

00:56.790 --> 00:59.750
See? You twist an apple
when you pick it, right?

00:59.750 --> 01:01.170
That's a good alteration.

01:01.170 --> 01:06.170
Changing up signs to suit your goal is
what makes spells infinitely adaptable.

01:08.870 --> 01:11.630
When something doesn't work,
figure out why you failed.

01:11.630 --> 01:14.290
And when you succeed,
ask, "Why did that work?"

01:14.290 --> 01:18.310
The purpose of repeating lessons
is trial and error!

01:18.310 --> 01:21.690
It's important not to just act
out of habit. Right, Master?

01:21.690 --> 01:23.440
Exactly right.

01:23.440 --> 01:26.740
You're an excellent teacher, Master Tetia.

01:28.030 --> 01:30.530
Master Tetia?!

01:31.050 --> 01:33.200
That's so sweet! I'm blushing!

01:33.200 --> 01:35.710
Do go on, now!

01:38.610 --> 01:41.740
Do you really have time
to be looking after others?

01:42.290 --> 01:44.760
If you're aware of your shortcomings,

01:44.760 --> 01:47.040
why not spend it on practice of your own?

01:51.170 --> 01:54.400
Okay, then! Show me how to do it!

01:54.400 --> 01:56.860
Hey, I wasn't telling you
to come over here!

01:56.860 --> 02:00.200
Let's go! Tetia Attack!

01:56.860 --> 02:00.200
I'm busy studying for my test,
so I don't have time to—

02:05.240 --> 02:10.030
So there are tests besides the Consent
of the Crown in the Dadah Range?

02:11.220 --> 02:12.140
Yes.

02:13.850 --> 02:16.460
Five of the stupid things
that don't matter.

02:16.460 --> 02:18.640
Like I need that garbage
to know how to draw...

02:19.260 --> 02:22.710
The point of the tests is to challenge
and learn about yourself.

02:23.030 --> 02:27.150
Whether or not they matter depends
on the attitude of the taker.

02:28.290 --> 02:34.080
Still, it's hard to enjoy things
you haven't chosen to take part in.

02:34.550 --> 02:38.100
The witches of old struggled
with that same problem.

02:38.100 --> 02:41.290
"Magic exists to make people happy.

02:41.290 --> 02:44.510
Making our apprentices suffer
would be missing the whole point."

02:44.510 --> 02:46.600
And so the Three Wise Ones thought it over

02:46.600 --> 02:49.440
and decided that the tests should
be adventures in the outside world

02:49.440 --> 02:51.940
that everyone would want to take.

02:55.260 --> 02:57.830
"Earn the permission to 
become an apprentice."

02:57.830 --> 03:00.500
The first test, the Consent of the Crown.

03:01.200 --> 03:03.540
"Display your devotion and
walk beside your master."

03:03.540 --> 03:06.370
The second test,
the Sincerity of the Shield.

03:07.290 --> 03:09.880
"Prove your path worthy
and take up the key."

03:09.880 --> 03:12.690
The third test, the Query of the Qui Vive.

03:13.410 --> 03:15.770
"Grant a wish and stand alone."

03:15.770 --> 03:18.840
The fourth test,
the Goodwill of Her Grace.

03:19.460 --> 03:21.920
"Now, you become the teacher."

03:21.920 --> 03:24.780
The fifth test, the Words of the Wise.

03:25.330 --> 03:28.120
This is the Pentacle of Proving.

03:28.690 --> 03:34.550
With each step you take,
you're allowed to do more with your magic.

03:34.550 --> 03:37.430
If you pass the fourth test,
you become a full-fledged witch

03:37.430 --> 03:39.700
and no longer need tutelage.

03:39.700 --> 03:42.220
You're allowed to take on 
the Tower of Tomes

03:42.220 --> 03:44.450
after passing the third test.

03:46.940 --> 03:49.830
The last test is for taking
your own apprentices,

03:49.830 --> 03:52.820
so you don't have to think about 
that until after you graduate.

03:52.820 --> 03:54.210
Aw...

03:54.210 --> 03:58.270
But I'm always thinking about what
I'm gonna do after I graduate!

03:58.270 --> 04:01.730
Traveling to faraway places,

04:01.730 --> 04:04.490
helping all kinds of people with magic,

04:04.490 --> 04:08.700
hearing "thank you" from 
people all over the world...

04:09.100 --> 04:13.230
One person says thank you,
and one person gets thanked!

04:13.550 --> 04:16.110
One little spell makes two people happy!

04:16.110 --> 04:18.360
What could be better than that?!

04:18.630 --> 04:20.110
Two birds with one stone!

04:20.110 --> 04:21.620
Two needs with one deed!

04:21.620 --> 04:24.270
Happiness comes in twos, like pigtails!

04:24.270 --> 04:25.370
Y'know?

04:25.370 --> 04:30.990
I can't wait to grow up and
design a cap with two points!

04:30.990 --> 04:33.040
Your hairstyle is actually symbolic?!

04:33.040 --> 04:36.980
You do get to choose your own cap
when you become a full-fledged witch.

04:37.380 --> 04:39.860
I hate tests.

04:40.760 --> 04:42.200
They're annoying.

04:42.200 --> 04:44.370
I hate people telling me what to do

04:44.370 --> 04:46.760
and making me draw spells
I don't want to draw.

04:47.150 --> 04:49.460
If you only draw the spells
you want to draw...

04:51.530 --> 04:55.020
you'll never learn anything new.

05:01.340 --> 05:02.880
Fine by me.

05:03.660 --> 05:08.200
If being an adult means having
to do things I don't want to do,

05:08.200 --> 05:10.230
I'll stay just as I am now.

05:11.120 --> 05:12.670
I'm leaving.

05:14.320 --> 05:15.620
Richeh...

05:15.620 --> 05:19.510
I refuse to stay as I am now.

05:19.510 --> 05:21.800
There are too many things I can't do yet.

05:22.290 --> 05:24.390
I want to take all the tests
as soon as possible.

05:24.860 --> 05:28.540
Then, someday, I'll become a
librarian in the Tower of Tomes.

05:29.270 --> 05:32.070
I wish I could grow up faster, even!

05:33.690 --> 05:38.750
Agott's family is descended from
an apprentice to the Three Wise Ones.

05:38.750 --> 05:40.780
They have librarians in every generation.

05:40.780 --> 05:44.030
I think it was... House Arklaum?

05:45.380 --> 05:48.550
<i>So Agott is also trying to get
to the Tower of Tomes...</i>

05:49.850 --> 05:50.980
What about you?

05:52.030 --> 05:54.770
What kind of witch do you want to be?

05:54.770 --> 05:58.300
I came from a different
starting point than you guys,

05:58.300 --> 06:00.780
so my path is pretty well laid out for me.

06:03.580 --> 06:07.680
For now, I just have to increase
the number of spells I can cast!

06:08.080 --> 06:11.970
Okay! I'll try that Grasping Wind
spell one more time!

06:11.970 --> 06:13.520
Yeah!

06:12.650 --> 06:14.140
<i>By drawing spells, you remember them.</i>

06:13.840 --> 06:15.830
Coco! Give me your hand!

06:14.140 --> 06:16.120
<i>By remembering them, 
you become able to use them.</i>

06:15.830 --> 06:16.790
Okay!

06:16.120 --> 06:21.210
<i>The power you acquire that 
way will never betray you.</i>

06:17.940 --> 06:20.370
One, two... upsy-daisy!

07:55.970 --> 07:58.150
What? Where is everyone?

07:58.580 --> 08:02.000
It's so dark... When did it become night?

08:02.440 --> 08:04.520
Coco? Coco!

08:08.990 --> 08:10.090
Coco.

08:12.610 --> 08:13.880
Mom!

08:14.180 --> 08:16.680
Mom! I'm sorry!

08:16.680 --> 08:19.520
It's all my fault.
I'm the one who did it.

08:19.520 --> 08:24.050
I didn't mean any harm, but I couldn't
give up on magic like you wanted...

08:27.550 --> 08:29.960
This is why I warned you, though.

08:31.250 --> 08:33.490
Normal people can't do magic.

08:35.360 --> 08:36.310
Mom...

08:36.310 --> 08:38.710
You ignorant Outsider.

08:39.180 --> 08:41.750
This is all your fault, Coco.

08:42.180 --> 08:44.400
Turning your mother to stone...

08:44.400 --> 08:47.020
Putting us all in danger...

08:47.020 --> 08:49.740
You're saying you didn't mean any of it?

08:51.380 --> 08:53.890
I don't want anything to do
with the Brimmed Caps.

08:53.890 --> 08:56.770
There are things that
some people just can't do.

08:56.770 --> 08:59.230
No exceptions can be made.

08:59.230 --> 09:01.830
It was kept a secret so
nothing like this would happen.

09:14.770 --> 09:18.160
This all happened
because you wanted magic.

09:18.160 --> 09:20.120
This is all your fault.

09:20.870 --> 09:23.890
And it'll be your fault
when the world falls apart!

09:49.770 --> 09:50.780
Master...

09:50.780 --> 09:52.180
You're still awake?

09:52.180 --> 09:54.030
I wanted more time to work, so...

09:54.030 --> 09:56.620
Stop that. Respect your limits.

09:56.620 --> 09:58.580
Yes, sir. I'll go back to bed.

10:06.840 --> 10:08.970
You're still awake, too?

10:09.410 --> 10:11.920
Yeah. I couldn't sleep.

10:17.890 --> 10:19.620
<i>By drawing, you remember.</i>

10:19.620 --> 10:21.370
<i>By remembering, you become able.</i>

10:21.930 --> 10:27.940
<i>How much more will I have to draw
before I can save my mom?</i>

10:36.660 --> 10:40.600
I've been waiting so long...
so very long...

10:43.870 --> 10:46.520
for this day to come...

10:47.630 --> 10:51.760
The Righteous Witches of Healingcraft,
who used magic to heal,

10:51.760 --> 10:53.640
fought the Three Wise Ones' edict

10:53.640 --> 10:57.340
forbidding spells cast on 
the body to the very end.

10:58.250 --> 10:59.230
The Twinned Bottles spell—

10:59.230 --> 11:02.430
a spell that allowed them to
share medicine among them—

11:02.430 --> 11:05.350
was lost when their memories were taken.

11:05.970 --> 11:08.870
No matter how far away one vial might be,

11:08.870 --> 11:13.130
its contents could be shared through
the seal-inscribed medal within,

11:13.130 --> 11:16.360
and they would never run
out of what they needed.

11:16.990 --> 11:22.100
A delicate spell of healing,
lost since the Day of the Pact...

11:22.540 --> 11:25.870
Ironic that only the Brimmed Caps
can create it now.

11:26.330 --> 11:29.470
You're a beautiful spell,
but I'll have to dissect you.

11:29.470 --> 11:32.180
You're the only connection I have to them.

11:33.880 --> 11:36.010
<i>I won't touch the Conjuring Ink yet.</i>

11:36.460 --> 11:38.530
<i>Its unknown power is too 
dangerous to tamper with.</i>

11:39.260 --> 11:44.520
<i>All I need is the inscribed
medal hidden within.</i>

11:44.520 --> 11:47.310
<i>Can I remove it without being detected?</i>

11:48.520 --> 11:50.960
<i>The medal within is tied to them.</i>

11:51.490 --> 11:54.820
<i>If I were to place it in a Guidance Orb,</i>

11:54.820 --> 11:58.220
<i>its components, its owner,
where it was made...</i>

11:58.220 --> 12:01.530
<i>Every trace of its existence
will point me toward them.</i>

12:02.450 --> 12:07.610
<i>I'll have a more concrete indication
of their location than any faint hints.</i>

12:15.440 --> 12:16.890
<i>A lightning spell?!</i>

12:16.890 --> 12:18.090
<i>They caught on!</i>

12:24.440 --> 12:25.770
<i>Water? Not good...</i>

12:36.910 --> 12:40.500
<i>I let my guard down.
I can't use spells underwater...</i>

13:12.130 --> 13:15.430
You're... the eyeball...

13:21.770 --> 13:24.510
W-Wait...

13:24.960 --> 13:26.260
Wait...

13:29.080 --> 13:32.830
I still have... to...

13:40.680 --> 13:43.690
Damn it. I won't give up.

13:44.590 --> 13:49.400
I will get back what was taken from me.

13:55.080 --> 13:57.780
After all the trouble to give it to her...

13:59.700 --> 14:01.360
What a waste.

14:12.910 --> 14:14.120
Synchronized yawns!

14:14.120 --> 14:15.810
You've been at it all day.

14:15.810 --> 14:17.520
Were you both up all night?

14:18.510 --> 14:19.470
I know!

14:19.470 --> 14:21.370
Night after night,
you transform into magic knights

14:21.370 --> 14:23.370
and fight off enemies with
your dazzling swordplay!

14:23.370 --> 14:25.780
Transformation spells are forbidden.

14:25.780 --> 14:29.970
Spending the day yawning is a sign
that you need to get more sleep.

14:30.550 --> 14:34.980
You've been up late practicing
these last few nights, right?

14:36.590 --> 14:39.610
Night's just when I feel
most inspired, I guess...

14:39.610 --> 14:41.610
You can't do that, Coco!

14:41.610 --> 14:44.620
I understand how you feel,
but it's not good to push yourself!

14:44.620 --> 14:46.920
Good magic demands good sleep.

14:46.920 --> 14:48.000
And food.

14:48.000 --> 14:50.100
Master Olly says it, too!

14:50.100 --> 14:53.870
If you don't get good sleep as a child,
you'll pay for it in your old age.

14:53.870 --> 14:55.120
Right?

14:55.120 --> 14:58.210
I'll make erbe tea to help you sleep!

14:58.210 --> 14:59.640
You want some, Master?

15:02.950 --> 15:04.130
Master?!

15:05.150 --> 15:07.140
Sorry, what were we talking about?

15:07.140 --> 15:08.630
I'm really sorry.

15:08.630 --> 15:11.000
I got so sleepy after just a few bites...

15:11.000 --> 15:12.730
I'll handle the tea.

15:14.510 --> 15:15.520
Hot!

15:19.390 --> 15:21.960
Master, are you sure you're all right?

15:21.960 --> 15:23.840
Yes, I'm fine.

15:25.740 --> 15:28.310
<i>I'm still numb from the lightning.</i>

15:29.030 --> 15:31.080
What a mess-up, huh?

15:31.080 --> 15:33.250
I ruined the last of our erbe tea.

15:33.250 --> 15:35.350
I'll go out and pick more leaves.

15:35.350 --> 15:38.290
Work on your Primers, everyone.

15:39.230 --> 15:41.600
I'll tidy up later,
so don't worry about it!

15:47.360 --> 15:49.450
Master's acting weird today!

15:49.450 --> 15:52.700
The effects of sleep deprivation
are not to be denied.

15:54.310 --> 15:56.730
I'll make him drink that erbe tea tonight.

15:56.210 --> 15:58.190
That's right. Agott...

15:56.730 --> 15:58.190
He needs to get some sleep!

15:58.190 --> 16:00.560
We'll get Master Olruggio to help, too.

15:58.190 --> 16:00.560
Can we talk for a minute?

16:05.790 --> 16:07.450
These are yours.

16:07.450 --> 16:09.670
My Sylph Shoes...

16:09.670 --> 16:12.200
I'm sorry it took so long to return them.

16:12.200 --> 16:15.560
It took a long time to 
get the seal just right.

16:17.130 --> 16:19.500
Is this what you were
working on last night?

16:21.010 --> 16:24.210
I'm sure the seal's not as good
as what you guys could do...

16:24.210 --> 16:27.010
If it's hard to fly with them,
feel free to redraw them.

16:31.730 --> 16:33.380
What's this all about?

16:35.280 --> 16:37.150
Just what are you plotting?

16:38.620 --> 16:40.500
I can't stop wondering.

16:40.500 --> 16:43.860
After the Consent of the Crown...
the first test...

16:44.280 --> 16:49.650
You never told Master Qifrey
that I forced you into it.

16:50.130 --> 16:53.180
You could have told Mister Olruggio, too.

16:53.880 --> 16:55.190
But...

16:55.190 --> 16:59.400
You never said a word against me,
and you even fixed my Sylph Shoes.

17:00.390 --> 17:05.880
Why? I just don't understand
what goes through your head.

17:08.180 --> 17:09.510
That day...

17:10.000 --> 17:12.140
You did force me,

17:12.140 --> 17:15.600
and the test was scary,
and I felt afraid all on my own.

17:16.700 --> 17:19.920
I could have just sat there and
waited for someone to get me.

17:20.980 --> 17:22.120
But...

17:23.700 --> 17:26.750
That day, as I stood at the 
base of the Dadah Range,

17:26.750 --> 17:29.530
it was me who decided to try it.

17:30.130 --> 17:35.530
I'm the one who wanted to prove that 
it was okay, and that I could do it.

17:36.080 --> 17:38.850
I wanted to overcome 
the trial with my own magic

17:38.850 --> 17:40.990
and feel like things
weren't totally hopeless.

17:43.120 --> 17:44.670
Because, otherwise...

17:49.250 --> 17:51.220
What are you saying, then?

17:51.220 --> 17:54.610
I'm the only one who's been
dwelling on it all this time?

17:54.610 --> 17:56.020
That's...

17:58.500 --> 17:59.500
Coco!

18:20.460 --> 18:23.450
Good, the feeling's come back.

18:24.890 --> 18:26.730
I wonder if they noticed
something was wrong.

18:26.730 --> 18:29.130
They're smart children, so maybe they did.

18:29.570 --> 18:31.250
If this gets out, it's over.

18:31.250 --> 18:33.630
I have to keep the secret.

18:34.080 --> 18:36.610
You won't tell anyone, right, Puffpuff?

18:37.890 --> 18:40.100
I guess you don't like that name.

18:42.350 --> 18:46.600
I thought it was cute, though... Puffpuff.

18:46.600 --> 18:47.860
So that's a no, huh?

18:48.610 --> 18:50.110
Master!

19:00.450 --> 19:02.890
You scared me, Agott!

19:02.890 --> 19:04.800
You were going so fast!

19:04.800 --> 19:09.130
The signs are too long,
so the Casting Seal is off-balance!

19:09.130 --> 19:11.550
Really? I'd love to have a look at it.

19:11.550 --> 19:13.910
No time for that! This is an emergency!

19:13.910 --> 19:15.110
It's Coco!

19:19.370 --> 19:21.220
I'll take her to the hospital in Kalhn.

19:21.220 --> 19:23.460
Sure. I'll watch the atelier.

19:23.460 --> 19:24.460
Thanks.

19:24.460 --> 19:27.700
If any of you need anything, talk to Olly.

19:40.930 --> 19:43.700
Hang in there.
We're almost at the hospital.

19:45.140 --> 19:47.260
<i>The fever's getting worse.</i>

19:47.260 --> 19:49.000
<i>She needs to see a doctor soon!</i>

19:56.600 --> 19:57.820
Okay, I'm next!

19:57.820 --> 19:58.660
You better get it right!

19:58.660 --> 20:00.100
Okay! Here I go!

20:01.050 --> 20:03.700
I've got you... There!

20:06.690 --> 20:08.420
You're supposed to catch it!

20:08.950 --> 20:10.770
Huh? Tartah, you're going already?

20:11.180 --> 20:14.120
Sorry, it's time for the ferry.

20:14.120 --> 20:17.280
Oh, yeah. You live on that sandbar, right?

20:17.710 --> 20:19.010
That's weird.

20:19.010 --> 20:22.780
If you're from a witch family,
why don't you just fly home?

20:22.780 --> 20:23.920
Yeah.

20:25.400 --> 20:28.790
There are rules to these things!

20:29.090 --> 20:30.220
Lame.

20:30.220 --> 20:31.650
Okay! See you tomorrow!

20:31.650 --> 20:33.150
Later!

20:37.000 --> 20:40.140
<i>People who don't know anything
sure love to mouth off.</i>

20:41.980 --> 20:43.550
<i>I would love to...</i>

20:48.170 --> 20:50.790
Huh? Mister Qifrey?

20:53.440 --> 20:54.410
What are you doing he—

20:54.410 --> 20:56.930
Tartah, the hospital 
is this way, isn't it?

20:57.330 --> 20:59.320
I don't know this area well.

20:59.910 --> 21:02.130
Oh, you want the hospital?

21:02.130 --> 21:04.360
This way. I know a shortcut.

21:04.720 --> 21:05.720
Thanks.

21:24.960 --> 21:26.060
Look after her.

21:26.060 --> 21:28.130
Yes, we will.

21:28.130 --> 21:29.850
Please wait.

21:33.220 --> 21:35.270
I hope she'll be all right.

21:35.970 --> 21:37.490
Thank you, Tartah.

21:37.940 --> 21:39.910
I'm so glad you knew the way.

21:40.340 --> 21:42.180
It's not that big a deal.

21:42.180 --> 21:43.870
No, it's quite impressive.

21:44.190 --> 21:46.870
You seem to be an observant person.

21:47.250 --> 21:49.730
I suppose you must look
at things very carefully.

21:53.150 --> 21:55.880
Hey, Mister Qifrey...

21:56.380 --> 22:00.250
There's a question I wanted to ask you.

23:35.390 --> 23:40.060
Episode 10:

23:35.390 --> 23:40.060
A Promise in Silver
